Strong 2-Minute Interview Answer

Dynamic Tables in Snowflake are automatically refreshed tables used for ELT pipelines. They simplify data engineering by removing the need for manually managing streams, tasks, and merge logic. Dynamic tables support incremental and full refresh modes and use TARGET_LAG to define data freshness requirements. They are commonly used in medallion architectures for bronze, silver, and gold transformations. Incremental refresh is preferred because it processes only changed data, improving performance and reducing compute costs.
